README.md
     1→# `sqlite-vec`
     5→An extremely small, "fast enough" vector search SQLite extension that runs
     6→anywhere! A successor to [`sqlite-vss`](https://github.com/asg017/sqlite-vss)
     7→
     8→<!-- deno-fmt-ignore-start -->
     9→
    10→> [!IMPORTANT]
    11→> _`sqlite-vec` is a pre-v1, so expect breaking changes!_
    12→
    13→<!-- deno-fmt-ignore-end -->
    14→
    15→- Store and query float, int8, and binary vectors in `vec0` virtual tables
    16→- Written in pure C, no dependencies, runs anywhere SQLite runs
    43→## Installing
    61→## Sample usage
    97→## Sponsors
   152→## See Also

ARCHITECTURE.md
     1→# `sqlite-vec` Architecture
     3→Internal documentation for how `sqlite-vec` works under-the-hood. Not meant for
     4→users of the `sqlite-vec` project, consult
     5→[the official `sqlite-vec` documentation](https://alexgarcia.xyz/sqlite-vec) for
     6→how-to-guides. Rather, this is for people interested in how `sqlite-vec` works
     7→and some guidelines to any future contributors.
     8→
     9→Very much a WIP.
    10→
    11→## `vec0`
    13→### Shadow Tables
    49→### idxStr

